 "note": "A StreamAudioDestination makes a real media stream (a MediaStreamAudioDestinationNode of the page's audio context): the children's sound goes into it through a gain stage, the stream is published in the page's stream table under every name in streamIdentifier (__bridge.snd.streams), isActive follows enabled, and gain and enabled act on the stream. Compared with the Web Audio specification, not with X_ITE: X_ITE 16.6.0 marks this node as not supported, keeps the fields, never sets isActive and makes no stream, so the test reads the stream back with a MediaStreamAudioSourceNode of the page (a 1 kHz sine of rms 0.7071 comes out at rms 0.7071 in the stream, gain 0.5 halves it, enabled = FALSE silences it, streamIdentifier moves the names) in our reader only, and the field and isActive lines that X_ITE can answer run in both.",
